response:
APT28 targeted a critical energy infrastructure facility in Ukraine using phishing emails delivering a malicious archive containing decoy images and scripts (associated with HeadLace malware). The attack leveraged legitimate web services like mockbin.org, mocky.io, webhook.site, and file.io along with living-off-the-land techniques (headless Microsoft Edge, wscript.exe, PowerShell) and Tor.

